@tradition book-circle
// Book circle: every other Monday (week 1 of two: days 15, 29, 43...; from day 8, so not in your arrival week), the
// junior common room on Deck 4. Bring a page you liked and read it aloud, or just listen. Matthias Oduya hosts.
// Added (not in the plan's table): Monday evenings had only running club, and a quiet, cozy evening suits the ship.
// The other Mondays of the four-week cycle have talent night (week 2) and the department cup (week 4).
k: 462
title: Book circle
when: every 2 weeks monday week 1 from day 8
at: 20:15-21:30
min: 25
jitter: 20
where: 4 pool common-room
where: 4 room Lift lobby: bench
who: oduya always, quiet-corner 55%, window-seat 35%, common-room 35%, everyone 15%
anim: read
host: oduya
from: oduya
invite: host=oduya odds=25% line="Book circle tonight. Bring a page you liked, or just come and listen."

== mail
- Book circle tomorrow, {time}, the junior common room. Bring a page you liked and read it to us, or just come and listen. There will be cocoa.

== ask
- Book circle tonight. I've marked my favourite page.
- I'm halfway through a very long book. Don't tell me the end.   #funny
- Book circle's nice. Nobody minds if you only listen.   #warm

== here
- Read that bit again?
- Oh, I like that.   #warm
- Shh. This is the good part.

== thanks
- You curl up in the common room while someone reads aloud. For an hour, the ship is very quiet.   #warm

== chatter
- Someone read a recipe at book circle. We all got hungry.   #funny
- We swap books after book circle. Mine came back with a pressed leaf in it.   #warm
- Matthias reads like it's a bedtime story. Best sleep I've had all week.   #funny
